# Yapo-only + A1 follow-up

Sibling sandbox of `portal_geo_am_v0_20261010`. Existing runs are reused and
immutable; no productive code is edited. Individual outputs remain encrypted
with Windows DPAPI CurrentUser. Aggregate results are in `results.json` and
`metrics.csv`; no confirmatory holdout or new source requests are used.

Yapo-only uses the exact original G3 folds (seeds 20261009/20261010), all 385 Yapo
targets and fixed previous adaptive A-M. AY = canonical A with Yapo training
pool; MY = adaptive A-M with Yapo pool; MM = reused adaptive A-M mixed pool;
A = reused original mixed canonical A. Training is source-filtered after the
signed custody release. Targets and dependency components are never regrouped.
Local branches coincide because the benchmark contains no Portal geography.
Three-way error metrics use the same supported targets; full coverage,
abstentions, 289 coordinates-present targets and 96 without coordinates are
separate. Repeated/centroid guards still allow fallback. Paired uncertainty uses
2000 draws of full dependency components, not independent-row resampling.

A1 is separate: the original canonical communal mixed-source A, all 791 targets,
unchanged native similarity functions, clipping, outliers, K20/min5 and surface
adjustment. Only five nonnegative weights summing to one change. There are 31
fixed vectors (original + 20 directed 0.1 transfers + 10 seeded Dirichlet draws).
Selection uses inner-only source-balanced MAE-log plus 0.1 times squared distance
from original weights; per-source coverage cannot fall below original A.
Each outer fold receives its own selected weights. No outer metrics generate
new vectors, tune regularization or select a single globally winning vector.
The same previously observed outer targets give exploratory evidence, not a
fresh independent validation. All31 vectors are checked against native A in
supplementary tests; only in-memory test constants change in that test process.

Portal verification: `oracle_status.json` records current checkout, container,
flags, systemd states and aggregate DB counts in a READ ONLY transaction. The
active card-first entrypoint fetches at most five **incomplete-card** details;
complete cards do not receive routine geography enrichment. Its timer is
inactive and Portal HTTP flag false. The generic refresh worker uses the list
parser for Portal detail pages. The experimental patch has no commit/integration
in the principal local repo, Oracle checkout or deployed image. Future detail
parsing, production rollout and historical recovery are separate actions;
none is executed here. Existing extraction already reads map_info.location;
the patch adds binding/provenance/precision and nondestructive propagation.

Reproduce with the existing research Python from workspace root; use a separate
copy/fresh output destination because overwriting encrypted runs is refused:

```powershell
$avmPython = 'work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Scripts/python.exe'
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/yapo_only.py 20261009
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/yapo_only.py 20261010
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/a1.py 20261009
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/a1.py 20261010
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/collect.py
python -B -c "import sys;sys.path.insert(0,'work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Lib/site-packages');import pytest;raise SystemExit(pytest.main(['research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/test_followup.py','research/portal_geo_am_followup_20261010/test_weight_math.py','-q','-p','no:cacheprovider']))"
```

Registration: the parent protocol's timestamp remains inherited in its copied
metadata; `registration_record.json` records the actual follow-up creation time
and protocol hash. The grid/objective were fixed before any follow-up result.
`execution_seal.json` locks prediction/tuning code; the supplementary test and
aggregate-only collector are included in the final delivery manifest.
